  "comments": "Date of Issue: 6th May, 1960<br /><br />\r\nHow to understand if 1961 is with “Fatha” in Arabic legend: small line over letter ra (ر‎) in “Israel”:<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5dcb203c6b82f.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5dcb203c6b82f.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n1974 bold and fine:<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/63f28d0fbe808.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/63f28d0fbe808.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5ef9dc5df1307.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5ef9dc5df1307.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nOf the coins dated 5721 (1961) without &quot;Fatha,&quot; 95,000 were minted by the Bern mint, 5,000,000 were minted by the Kings Norton Mint, and 7,726,000 were minted by the Jerusalem Mint.<br />\r\nOf the coins dated 5732 (1972), 1,260,000 were minted by the Jerusalem Mint and 18,393,112 were minted by the Bern Mint.<br />\r\nOf the coins dated 5733 (1973), 5,625,000 were minted by the Jerusalem Mint and 10,580,000 were minted by the Ottawa Mint.<br />\r\nOf the coins dated 5734 (1974), 3,880,000 were minted by the Jerusalem Mint and 18,160,000 were minted by the Ottawa Mint.<br />\r\nOf the coins dated 5736 (1976), 34,870,000 were minted by the Jerusalem Mint and 20,000,000 were minted by the Ottawa Mint.",
